{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["And Rashi explained: <b>mouth to mouth I speak with him</b> — to separate from his wife, as it is said: ״ואתה פה עמוד עמדי״. And if you ask: if so, why did they complain about what he separated? The answer: they complained about what he separated previously, before the Holy One, blessed be He, had commanded him to separate — had he not separated of his own accord. For we maintain: in the way a person wants to go, they lead him. And through the incident of Eldad and Medad they learned from the mouth of Zipporah that he had separated previously, as Rashi explained, and then they spoke of it."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:19.184404583Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}